+    "\n",
+    "Since HADDOCK3 version 2026.9.0 it is possible to perform a mutation scan of the DNA using the `dnascan` module. This will by default scan all possible base-pairs (DA-DT, DT-DA, DC-DG, DG-DC). Mutations are thus introduced in pairs to avoid disturbing the Waston-Crick base-pairing.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This provides a way of exploring interface energetics of the DNA.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "This module mutates the DNA base-pairs at the interface and calculates the **Δ HADDOCK score** between the wild-type and mutant, thus providing a measure of the impact of each base-pair mutation. It is possible to scan all interface residues one by one or limit this scanning to a selected by user set of residues. By default, all possible base-pairs are scanned.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Important**: \n",
